On 16.09.2014 02:31, Sonicdude5787 wrote:
> I died on dungeon level 1 from poisoning by a corpse. Explains a lot.
> Any advice for me?

Depends on whether you want to get spoiled or learn by exploration of
the game. In case of your early dying four short tips. Don't eat the
corpses that you noticed in previous games to not be healthy (you may
also watch what sort of corpses your pet eats). Then, fighting is not
always the best you can do, specifically if you are low on hitpoints;
retreat in corridors to not get surrounded, or change level (not all
monsters will follow you). Depending on your character class played
you may use missile weapons from distance; it's advantageous to fight
from distance instead of meleeing, or to weaken foes before meleeing.
Finally, let your pets help you fight; this means that you can dance
around your pet or retreat behind your pet in a corridor to avoid any
attacks.

There's a couple advice that are often given in case players know the
very basics, like: don't drink from fountains when you cannot handle
the bad effects, don't read unidentified scrolls or quaff unidentified
potions. But since you are a beginner you may want to experiment and
experience the [good and bad] effects yourself.

Last but not least, read the official Guidebook that comes with the
game; it has some helpful information for the first steps.

If you have more question feel free to ask.

